{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHFpQmnGcMpoVZnKyJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VvHj9XF79U67dsc9hvUnbg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='gen.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}''','''    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\n\n    The lower bound must be `start`, not `value`: Intervals exports\n    {value, end} as a zone-mapped (Lap HR) target that the watch clamps to its\n    own HR zones, while {start, end} exports as an Instant-HR corridor with the\n    bpm Intervals computed from its own LTHR.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | grep -A4 '\"hr\"' | head -12"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":24501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a78f5eb8-2c98-44c9-929f-20034afa9a3e","uuid":"e6084633-132f-4fc7-9df1-1052be47e649","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:04:32.472Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHFp99epbi1YTQJaVQB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VvHj9XF79U67dsc9hvUnbg":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-121MIy && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='gen.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}''','''    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\n\n    The lower bound must be `start`, not `value`: Intervals exports\n    {value, end} as a zone-mapped (Lap HR) target that the watch clamps to its\n    own HR zones, while {start, end} exports as an Instant-HR corridor with the\n    bpm Intervals computed from its own LTHR.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | grep -A4 '\"hr\"' | head -12"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01VvHj9XF79U67dsc9hvUnbg":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-121MIy"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VvHj9XF79U67dsc9hvUnbg","type":"tool_result","content":"        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n--\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"start\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n--","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a78f5eb8-2c98-44c9-929f-20034afa9a3e","uuid":"32a70a85-1017-4693-a772-37e3359fc825","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:04:33.008Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n--\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"start\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n--","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-121MIy/gen.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":9,"newStart":8,"newLines":15,"lines":[" "," "," def hr_target(step):","-    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"","+    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.","+","+    The lower bound must be `start`, not `value`: Intervals exports","+    {value, end} as a zone-mapped (Lap HR) target that the watch clamps to its","+    own HR zones, while {start, end} exports as an Instant-HR corridor with the","+    bpm Intervals computed from its own LTHR.","+    \"\"\"","     lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]","-    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}","+    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}"," "," "," def build_step(step):"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-121MIy/gen.py"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VvHj9XF79U67dsc9hvUnbg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHGK9fcW7dDox3BMGdt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BvDWkNTKWwY4kGvsz1kWCX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-121MIy/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to watch zones: what changed\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the HR target now uses `start` for the lower bound instead of `value`:\n\n```diff\n-    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n+    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n```\n\nNothing else changed. The targets are still percentages of LTHR, so Intervals still converts them to bpm with its own LTHR (172) when it exports.\n\n## Why\n- In Intervals.icu's `workout_doc`, the name of the lower-bound key decides how the HR target is exported to the FIT file:\n  - `{value, end}` becomes a zone-mapped (Lap HR) target. The Garmin snaps it to its own HR zones, which come from its auto-detected LTHR of 168. That is exactly what `readback/watch-notes.md` shows: every step displays one of the watch's own zone bands (118–137, 137–151, 151–162), and changing the watch's LTHR only moves the bands.\n  - `{start, end}` becomes an Instant-HR corridor. The watch shows the bpm range Intervals computed, e.g. Float 75–82% → 129–141.\n- Your earlier attempts fit this explanation. `units: \"bpm\"` was read as a percentage (214–249). `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` aren't fields Intervals knows, so they were dropped and the watch fell back to its default (101).\n- Source: this came from the worklore story *\"Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\"*. It describes the same symptom with the same numbers (LTHR 172 in Intervals, 168 on the watch). I couldn't check it against the Intervals API docs or a real device from here.\n\n## Not verified\nI didn't push anything. To confirm the fix, run `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`, sync the watch and check that the steps show 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124 bpm.\n\n## Other things I noticed (left unchanged)\n- **The web UI may not show the steps.** The same story says the Intervals web UI renders steps from a separate top-level `description` written in Intervals' text format. That text has its own pitfalls: `m` means minutes, and a bare `Z2` is read as a power zone. The watch export doesn't need it, so I didn't add it.\n- **API keys are committed to the repo.** They are in `README.md` and `config/intervals.toml`, both tracked by git. You should rotate them and move them into `.env` (already gitignored).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633,"cache_read_input_tokens":26574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":633},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a78f5eb8-2c98-44c9-929f-20034afa9a3e","uuid":"9bfce46b-e2ef-4913-be05-1b7cb19132a8","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:04:42.879Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHGJw269N2ag1gi3qzV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BvDWkNTKWwY4kGvsz1kWCX":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-121MIy/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to watch zones: what changed\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the HR target now uses `start` for the lower bound instead of `value`:\n\n```diff\n-    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n+    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n```\n\nNothing else changed. The targets are still percentages of LTHR, so Intervals still converts them to bpm with its own LTHR (172) when it exports.\n\n## Why\n- In Intervals.icu's `workout_doc`, the name of the lower-bound key decides how the HR target is exported to the FIT file:\n  - `{value, end}` becomes a zone-mapped (Lap HR) target. The Garmin snaps it to its own HR zones, which come from its auto-detected LTHR of 168. That is exactly what `readback/watch-notes.md` shows: every step displays one of the watch's own zone bands (118–137, 137–151, 151–162), and changing the watch's LTHR only moves the bands.\n  - `{start, end}` becomes an Instant-HR corridor. The watch shows the bpm range Intervals computed, e.g. Float 75–82% → 129–141.\n- Your earlier attempts fit this explanation. `units: \"bpm\"` was read as a percentage (214–249). `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` aren't fields Intervals knows, so they were dropped and the watch fell back to its default (101).\n- Source: this came from the worklore story *\"Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\"*. It describes the same symptom with the same numbers (LTHR 172 in Intervals, 168 on the watch). I couldn't check it against the Intervals API docs or a real device from here.\n\n## Not verified\nI didn't push anything. To confirm the fix, run `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`, sync the watch and check that the steps show 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124 bpm.\n\n## Other things I noticed (left unchanged)\n- **The web UI may not show the steps.** The same story says the Intervals web UI renders steps from a separate top-level `description` written in Intervals' text format. That text has its own pitfalls: `m` means minutes, and a bare `Z2` is read as a power zone. The watch export doesn't need it, so I didn't add it.\n- **API keys are committed to the repo.** They are in `README.md` and `config/intervals.toml`, both tracked by git. You should rotate them and move them into `.env` (already gitignored).\n"}}}
